cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Speak Before the Reveal: cheat sheet skill and worked examples"
message: "If you use this skill or the cheat sheets, please cite both this repository and the method paper."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Jurblum
    given-names: Marc
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-2208-7042"
abstract: >-
  An LLM skill that interviews a clinician and builds a printable reference
  guide for use with an AI scribe, together with three worked examples, in
  psychiatry, general medicine and general practice. The guide prompts the
  clinician to dictate their clinical reasoning while the scribe is still
  recording, before it generates its note, so that the reasoning is authored
  rather than edited. The method is a reasoned precaution and has not been
  evaluated in a trial.
keywords:
  - AI scribe
  - ambient documentation
  - clinical reasoning
  - deskilling
  - cognitive offloading
  - clinical documentation
  - workforce capability
  - health informatics
  - artificial intelligence
  - clinical governance
  - automation bias
